maria: Heads up — client-js v17.0.0 published to npm. Leaving a quick roundup of breaking changes + mitigation steps. Please react/flag anything missing.

maria: TL;DR: auth param rename, streaming method rename, retry policy change, Node/packaging updates, and a cache layout note. Small patches recommended for internal services before we recommend customer-wide upgrade. :eyes:

maria: 1) Auth: SDK now standardizes on `token` / Authorization: Bearer <token>. `apiKey` / X-API-KEY usage is deprecated and will be removed in v18. We ship a compatibility shim for 17.x but encourage migrating.

maria: 2) Streaming: `client.stream(...)` is renamed to `client.chat.stream(...)` and yields a slightly different event shape (delta/meta events separated). Old iterator will still work behind a compatibility flag, but we should update examples and quickstarts.

maria: 3) Retries: default retry behavior tightened to only auto-retry idempotent endpoints. Previously the client retried many endpoints by default which masked some server-side errors. To opt out/restore old behavior in 17.x you can set env `REDWOOD_SDK_LEGACY_RETRIES=true` or pass per-client option `retries: { mode: 'legacy' }`.

maria: 4) Node + packaging: minimum supported Node >=16, Node 18+ recommended for the ESM-first build. The package ships ESM entrypoint by default; CJS shim is available but will be removed in 18.x.

maria: 5) Cache/layout: the local KV cache binary format changed — when upgrading runtime we recommend nuking the on-disk KV cache (or bumping the cache version) to avoid corrupted KV lookups. See note below.

kevin: Confirming Node support and cache: +1 on Node 16 min, recommend teams test under Node 18. I'll run the perf/integration suite tomorrow. For the KV cache: we'll add a cache-version header so upgraded clients automatically invalidate stale stores.

lina: I opened a migration guide PR with examples for each language (node snippet + python note) — https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/1523 :book: lmk if the wording is okay.

sam: Canary plan idea: roll to 10% hosted traffic tomorrow, dedicated customers are opt-in only. We'll watch latency/error deltas and token spend. Can we add a short eval that checks streaming event shapes?

maria: Good call. Sample migration snippet for Node (please paste into docs):

```js
// old (pre-17.x)
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY });
for await (const chunk of client.stream({ model: 'rw-large', input: 'hi' })) {
  // process chunk
}

// new (17.x)
const client = new Redwood({ token: process.env.REDWOOD_TOKEN, retries: { mode: 'none' } });
const stream = await client.chat.stream({ model: 'rw-large', input: 'hi' });
for await (const evt of stream) {
  if (evt.type === 'delta') process.stdout.write(evt.delta);
  if (evt.type === 'meta') console.log('meta', evt);
}
```

kevin: Note: if you rely on the old `apiKey` param, the compatibility shim will translate it to `Authorization` for now, but log a one-time warning. Recommend switching env var name to REDWOOD_TOKEN to make your infra explicit.

lina: Docs PR updated with the snippet and a migration checklist. I also added a compatibility section with the env flag example: `REDWOOD_SDK_LEGACY_RETRIES=true` and the deprecation schedule.

sam: QA + monitoring notes: add a regression eval that asserts streaming event ordering and a token-count smoke test. I'll add a PromQL alert for streaming-error-rate > 0.5% during canary window.

maria: Also — code-review ping @kevin for the runtime change that bumps cache version (PR #4876). We need that merged before we flip the canary. :pray:

devex-bot: PR merged: docs migration guide (#1523) -> deployed to staging. Link: https://staging.docs.redwood.ai/migration/17

deploy-bot: Canary rollout scheduled: hosted-api v17 -> 10% at 2026-03-18T15:00Z (UTC).

kevin: I'll run the bench + integration tests and post results here. If anyone has services that must preserve the old cache format, please reply so we can add an escape hatch.

maria: Thanks everyone. If you touch examples or quickstarts, update them to `client.chat.stream` and `token` param. I'll assemble a short changelog note for the public release. :shipit:
